WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.349
I'm not a fraud.

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.239
I'm not a criminal

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.159
who defrauded the entire country

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.539
and made up this fictitional

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.489
character and ran for Congress.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.079
I've been around a long time.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.819
That's newly elected New York

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.739
Congressman George Santos

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.629
apologizing after getting

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.429
caught, lying about where he went to

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.559
high school and whether he graduated

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.779
from college and where he worked

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.479
after not graduating from college

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.399
and whether he's Brazilian or

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.859
Jewish and whether his grandparents

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.869
actually fled the Holocaust

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.849
and whether his mother died

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.829
on 9/11.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.719
Santos is an extreme case,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.549
but resume padding is nothing

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.319
new in Washington.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.909
Who can forget Senator Elizabeth

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.919
Warren's fraudulent and ultimately

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.869
apologized-for claims to Native

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.099
American heritage?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.719
I am not a person of color.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.549
I am not a citizen

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.959
of a tribe.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.059
She apparently even plagiarized

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.279
the Cherokee recipes

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.229
she contributed to the 1984

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.659
cookbook called Pow Wow Chow.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.129
There's folks like Senator Dick

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.989
Blumenthal of Connecticut who lied

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.488
about serving in Vietnam during a

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:06.899
tight race, but well, you know,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.489
really didn't do anything wrong.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.149
Right?

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.189
I may have misspoken.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.109
I did meet misspeak

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.909
on a few occasions.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.499
And, of course, there's President

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.329
Biden who dropped out of his

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.219
1988 presidential bid

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.589
after getting caught lying about his

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.899
undistinguished academic record.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.669
Graduated with three degrees from

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.799
undergraduate school, 165 credits,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.239
only needed 123 credits.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.949
Biden now concedes he did not

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.569
graduate in the top half of his law

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.339
school class, that he does not have

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.199
three degrees from college and that

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.489
he was not named outstanding

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.779
political science student.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.299
Incredibly, he even plagiarized

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.769
the life story of a British

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.599
politician whose families were

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.799
coal miners.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.449
Hell, I might be president now if it

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.279
weren't for the fact I said my, I

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.699
had an uncle who was a coal miner

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.709
turned out I didn't have anybody in
the

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.209
coal mines, you know, I mean.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.283
I tried that crap, you know.

00:01:55.284 --> 00:01:56.909
When politicians invent

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.589
accomplishments and lie about their

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.479
past, it reflects poorly on their

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.099
character, and it shows of

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.049
willingness to cheat in the pursuit

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.339
of power.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.529
But the most harmful falsehoods

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.569
that politicians tell aren't

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.008
about the scholarships they didn't

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:13.139
win, the wars they didn't fight

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.239
or the discrimination they didn't

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.409
overcome.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.079
They're about the laws they passed.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.149
Consider last summer's stupendously

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.489
misnamed Inflation Reduction Act,

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.199
which the president announced would

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.479
shrink the budget deficit and reduce

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.619
rising prices.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.929
This bill, this bill

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.179
will reduce inflationary pressures

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.679
on the economy.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.569
This bill will, in fact,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.860
reduce inflationary

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.420
pressure on the economy.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.559
Even outlets sympathetic to Biden

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.029
weren't buying that.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.499
What the bill actually does is

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.329
create a vast number of tax breaks

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.489
and incentives aimed at greening

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.839
the economy.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.699
It raises taxes enough to reduce

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.549
the deficit by around 300 billion,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.409
which is just 2% of planned

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.719
borrowing over the next ten years.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.759
It does nothing to reduce our

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.249
$30 trillion in debt.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.779
Who's loaning the US government

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.829
those funds?

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.869
The Federal Reserve, mostly, which

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.669
pays for all those Treasury bonds by

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.499
printing money out of thin air: the

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.169
principal cause of inflation.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.449
When he took office, the ten-year

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.579
deficit was expected to be

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.039
$12.2 trillion.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.873
By the end of his first year, it had

00:03:24.874 --> 00:03:27.219
climbed to a projected 14.5

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.889
trillion.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.779
He's also misrepresented his record

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.669
on job creation, tweeting in

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.499
September that, "Right now

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.879
I have the strongest record on

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.099
growing manufacturing jobs in modern

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.199
history." As The Washington

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.239
Post Glenn Kessler pointed out,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.069
Richard Nixon beats Biden

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.479
handily on that count with 1.3

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.419
million new manufacturing jobs

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.309
back in the early seventies, when

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.229
the country was a lot smaller,

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.289
to Biden's 630,000.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.759
Biden also promised that it would

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.739
end his predecessor's use of Title

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.869
42 rules to keep migrants

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.429
from Latin America from entering the

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.379
country while seeking asylum

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.249
here.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.469
His flip-flop on that has alienated

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.529
even his most ardent supporters.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.389
Of course, Joe Biden hardly

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.789
invented political lying, especially

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.899
among presidents.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.789
Indeed, his predecessors in the

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.159
Oval Office lied about everything,

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.169
everywhere, all at once; health

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.839
care policy; pretext for war;

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.189
and sex.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.349
I did not have

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.109
sexual relations with that woman,

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.069
Miss Lewinsky.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.959
From newly minted congressmen like

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.669
George Santos to the president,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.679
we've come to expect and maybe

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.959
even accept that our politicians

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.639
are going to lie about their resumes

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:42.989
and their personal lives.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.539
That is totally unacceptable.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.919
But it's the lies about their

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.899
policies that we really

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.729
end up paying for and

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.320
that we really can't afford.

